 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Hotel manager Mikhail Jekovich knocks on the room door because guests are complaining about the noise. When Mikhail keeps poking around, Senya knocks him out with another vase, and Chef Barinov forbids any more violence.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Постояльцы жалуются на сильный шум.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А что ты тут делаешь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я принёс блюдо от шефа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А кто там громко мычит?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Это просто от большого удовольствия.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Всё, быстро иди отсюда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Кажется, мы тут не спалились.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Зачем ты суёшь свой нос?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Надо что-то решать, шеф.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "У нас уже вазы кончаются.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Он сам от ревности повесился.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Никто сегодня здесь не умрёт!",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Постояльцы жалуются на сильный шум.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The hotel guests are complaining about loud noise.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'hotel guests' before landing on 'noise'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А что ты тут делаешь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And what are you doing here?' The meaning hinges on 'and' working together with 'are doing' in spoken Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Я принёс блюдо от шефа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I brought a dish from the chef.' Fedya brings out the contrast between 'I' and 'brought' in a few short words. Mikhail answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "А кто там громко мычит?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And who is mooing loudly in there?' Mikhail brings out the contrast between 'and' and 'who' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Это просто от большого удовольствия.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That is just from great pleasure.' The grammar packs 'this' and 'pleasure' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Всё, быстро иди отсюда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'That is it, go away from here quickly.' The meaning hinges on 'everything' working together with 'from here' in spoken Russian. Fedya answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Кажется, мы тут не спалились.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'It seems we did not get caught here.' Fedya brings out the contrast between 'it seems' and 'we' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Зачем ты суёшь свой нос?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why do you poke your nose everywhere?' The meaning hinges on 'why' working together with 'nose' in spoken Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Надо что-то решать, шеф.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We need to decide something, Chef.' Notice how Russian expresses 'need' and 'to decide' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "У нас уже вазы кончаются.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We are already running out of vases.' The meaning hinges on 'at' working together with 'are running out' in spoken Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Он сам от ревности повесился.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He hanged himself out of jealousy.' The '-l' ending on the verb meaning 'hanged himself' places the action in the masculine past tense.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Никто сегодня здесь не умрёт!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nobody is going to die here today!' The meaning hinges on 'nobody' working together with 'will die' in spoken Russian. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
